xnu 0483: start the wifi worker right after the usb probe

Measured 2026-11-26 with the stage counter: `wifistage 1` on 0481/0482 -- the
boot premap ran, the worker never reached stage 2. The worker start is the last
statement of the probe block, and the block stops in the audio/Venus/BT tail
when the pin premap runs first. `0480` reached `worker started` with the start
inside `mondrian_usb_probe()`, and `0481` mapped the pins before touch.

Both proven halves are combined: the pins stay premapped at the top, and the
worker starts right after `mondrian_usb_probe()`. It takes no `ml_io_map()` of
its own, so it cannot race the tail that follows.
diff --git a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
index 5379e5e..4c8bd7a 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -2417,18 +2417,19 @@ mondrian_log_start(void)
 		(void)mondrian_gpu_probe();
 		mondrian_touch_probe();
 		mondrian_usb_probe();
+		/*
+		 * Start here, before the audio/Venus/BT tail: the block has been
+		 * measured to stop in that tail when the pin premap runs first
+		 * (0481/0482: `wifistage 1`, the worker never reached stage 2),
+		 * while starting inside `usb_probe` reached `worker started`
+		 * (0480). Every window the worker uses is premapped above, so it
+		 * takes no ml_io_map() and cannot race the tail.
+		 */
+		mondrian_wifi_start();
 		mondrian_audio_probe_start();
 		mondrian_venus_start();
 		mondrian_bt_tty_init();
 		mondrian_bt_ctl_init();
-		/*
-		 * Last, with the whole probe block done: the worker maps the
-		 * TLMM pin pages itself, and mapping them at the top of the
-		 * block or beside a probe that is still mapping wedges the
-		 * mapper (measured 2026-11-26, five boots stopped at a
-		 * different point each time).
-		 */
-		mondrian_wifi_start();
 	}
 }
 
